<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Stettin (1570)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1570">1570</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Stettin (1570) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-seven-years-war">Northern Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Stettin, signed on 13 December 1570, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-seven-years-war">Northern Seven Years' War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>. Neither side made lasting territorial gains: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> gave up its claims to Sweden, Sweden renounced its claims to Norway and other Danish lands, and Sweden agreed to pay a large ransom to recover the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvsborg">Älvsborg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stettin-1570.jpg" alt="Treaty of Stettin (1570)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: various · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StettinPeacesignatures.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
